title: Implement passive c2c ingress through app-server thread injection
---
Depends on the protocol spike and managed remote-TUI launcher.

Create a c2c adapter that writes an inbound message to the durable broker inbox first, then uses only the validated `thread/inject_items` form to make it model-visible without starting or steering a turn.

Acceptance criteria:
- Never use PTY writes, `tmux send-keys`, Herdr pane run, `turn/start`, `turn/steer`, or `turn/interrupt` for passive delivery.
- Preserve c2c envelope, sender attribution, ephemeral/archive behavior, and the bus-not-RPC invariant.
- Make retry/idempotency and app-server disconnection behavior explicit; messages remain readable from the broker on every failure.
- Feature-gate the integration by proven Codex version/capabilities and retain hooks as fallback.

Blockers: P1.M1.E1.T001 protocol result and P1.M1.E1.T002 live remote-TUI lifecycle.